.TH GRINTION-SECURITY 1 "November 2026" "Grintion-OS" "Security Administration"
.SH NAME
grintion-security \- Security hardening profile manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grintion-security
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B grintion-security
manages and applies defense-in-depth system security profiles for Grintion-OS, orchestrating firewall policies, AppArmor enforcement, USB data-blocking, and audit availability.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Show active profile and compliance state.
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List available security profiles (workstation, server, kiosk, air-gapped).
.TP
\fBset\fR \fIPROFILE\fR [\fB--config-only\fR]
Apply the profile firewall, AppArmor and USB policy, write profile state, and
verify the running result. A failed control rolls back the profile files and
firewall. \fB--config-only\fR writes configuration without activating controls.
.TP
\fBverify\fR
Validate the active firewall chain, AppArmor enforcement, USB state and auditd
availability. Auditd is reported as a warning when its userspace is not
installed in the base image.
.TP
\fBapply-firewall\fR
Apply the policy recorded in \fBsecurity.conf\fR. Used by the boot firewall
service; exits non-zero when validation or application fails.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--json\fR
Emit machine-readable output where supported.
.SH AUTHORS
Grintion-OS Core Team.

